      "term": "seric iron",
      "matchText": "seric iron",
      "definition": "The Roman name for high-grade steel imported from the East — literally \"iron of the Seres,\" the Seres being the Greco-Roman term for the silk-trading peoples of Asia, vaguely associated with China. The label was a misnomer: the steel actually came from India (Maurya-era and later wootz/crucible steel), but Roman writers were hazy about Asian geography and assumed anything exotic from the East was \"Chinese.\"",
      "type": "concept"
