      "term": "Brahmanical revival",
      "matchText": "Brahmanical revival",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "A resurgence of Vedic-Brahmin religious authority — temple ritual, animal sacrifice, and the varna (caste) order administered by the priestly Brahmin class — after the Maurya period. Under the Shungas the state shifted patronage back toward this orthodoxy and away from Ashoka’s non-sectarian dhamma, though Buddhist institutions kept flourishing alongside it."
